sh_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:d3577969cf44d21d2b03e8f05bafda8edfd977a870d3a96782b92277615e4655","file":"preprints/A-continuum-temperature-singularity-for-a-radial-pair-potential-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":44,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"633486bc3b291b0f8b9d1731ecac055e88c24329035c34840d8f788ac988b55f","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-continuum-temperature-singularity-for-a-radial-pair-potential-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:d3577969cf44d21d2b03e8f05bafda8edfd977a870d3a96782b92277615e4655","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-continuum-temperature-singularity-for-a-radial-pair-potential-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L44"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere exist an admissible radial difference-only pair potential\n$\\Phi(x)=\\phi(|x|)$ on $\\R^3$, a nonempty open interval\n$I\\subset(0,\\infty)$, and one $\\beta_c\\in(1/2,3/2)$ with the following\nproperties. The potential satisfies $\\phi(r)=o(r^{-3})$ as $r\\to\\infty$.\nThe free-cube limit \\eqref{eq:free-energy-definition} exists and is finite\nfor every $\\beta>0$ and every density $\\rho>0$. For every $\\rho\\in I$,\nthe finite one-sided derivatives at the same critical point satisfy\n\\[\n D_\\beta^- f_\\Phi(\\beta_c,\\rho)\n >D_\\beta^+ f_\\Phi(\\beta_c,\\rho).\n\\]\nThus one potential and one critical inverse temperature give a strict\ncanonical temperature singularity throughout $I$."}
